  "issue_title": "[bug] Frozen LiveCodeBench-v6 items are unscoreable: score_text raises \"Unknown benchmark 'livecodebench_v6'\"",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\nThe LiveCodeBench-v6 adapter serialises its release **identity** as the frozen item's `benchmark` field:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/adapters/livecodebench.py  (serialize_task)\n\"benchmark\": self.name,   # -> \"livecodebench_v6\"\n```\n\nThis is intentional and pinned by `tests/test_livecodebench_v6_adapter.py::test_serialize_task_is_json_safe_and_versioned` (the frozen item must record which release produced it). The value survives the whole hidden-benchmark pipeline: `from_adapter_task` copies `serialized[\"benchmark\"]`, and `to_protocol_item` carries it to the on-disk protocol item.\n\nBut `reward.score_text` / `reward.has_answer` dispatch on **family** keys and only know the bare names in the frozensets (`CODE_BENCHMARKS = {\"livecodebench\", \"lcb\", \"bigcodebench\", \"bigcode\"}`). `\"livecodebench_v6\"` is in none of them, so:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/orchestration/reward.py  (score_text)\nif key in CODE_BENCHMARKS: ...\nraise ValueError(f\"Unknown benchmark {benchmark!r}. ...\")\n```\n\nEvery place that scores a frozen v6 item hits this:\n- `scripts/pr_eval.py::_evaluate_cached` \u2192 `score_text(canonical[\"benchmark\"] or \"math500\", ...)`\n- `scripts/pr_eval.py::_evaluate_live` \u2192 sets `benchmark=canonical[\"benchmark\"]`, then `score(traj)`\n\nSo building a hidden benchmark from the v6 adapter (`python scripts/build_benchmark.py --benchmark livecodebench_v6`, a directly-selectable, registered adapter) produces frozen items that make `pr_eval` **crash on the first item** with `ValueError: Unknown benchmark 'livecodebench_v6'`, aborting the whole evaluation.\n\nThe adapter is internally consistent otherwise \u2014 `score_output` and `load_tasks` already use the shared `base_benchmark = \"livecodebench\"`; only the frozen-item identity carries the versioned name, and the scorer has no way to map it back to the family.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n- *Expected:* a frozen LiveCodeBench-v6 item scores through the LiveCodeBench code checker (the item's `dataset_version` / `meta[\"adapter\"]` still record the v6 release).\n- *Actual:* `score_text` / `has_answer` raise `ValueError: Unknown benchmark 'livecodebench_v6'`; `pr_eval` aborts.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\n```python\nfrom trinity.orchestration.reward import score_text\n\nspec = {\"tests\": [{\"input\": \"3\\n\", \"output\": \"9\"}]}\ncode = \"n = int(input())\\nprint(n * n)\\n\"\nscore_text(\"livecodebench_v6\", code, spec)   # ValueError: Unknown benchmark 'livecodebench_v6'\n```\n\nOr end-to-end:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/build_benchmark.py --benchmark livecodebench_v6 ...   # freezes items with benchmark=\"livecodebench_v6\"\npython scripts/pr_eval.py --pr <n> --benchmark livecodebench_v6 ...  # aborts on the first item\n```\n\n**Environment**\n- Python version: 3.10+\n- GPU: CPU only (pure/offline reward path; pass@1 runs in a subprocess sandbox)\n- Commit hash: current `main` (`c23c767`)\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-10T19:36:40.000Z",
